    {
      "id": "i2c_lcd1602",
      "name": "16x2 LCD with I2C Backpack",
      "category": "Display",
      "subcategory": "Character LCD",
      "description": "16x2 character LCD with a PCF8574 I2C backpack (4-pin header).",
      "keywords": ["lcd", "1602", "i2c", "pcf8574", "display"],
      "protocols": ["I2C"],
      "interfaces": ["I2C"],
      "pins": [
        {"name": "VCC", "type": "power"}, {"name": "GND", "type": "ground"},
        {"name": "SDA", "type": "bidirectional"}, {"name": "SCL", "type": "input"}
      ],
      "model": {"shape": "lcd1602_i2c"},
      "mounting": "module",
      "simulation_status": "external",
      "simulation_models": ["hd44780-i2c"],
      "simulation_backend": "firmware",
      "arduino_compatible": true,
      "params": {
        "address": {"default": 39, "label": "I2C address (7-bit)"},
        "cols": {"default": 16, "label": "Columns", "min": 1, "max": 40},
        "rows": {"default": 2, "label": "Rows", "min": 1, "max": 4}
      },
      "notes": "No breadboard electrical model: the harness decodes the HD44780 4-bit protocol from the backpack's PCF8574 writes (RS/RW/E/backlight + D4..D7) and returns the visible text in run_firmware's devices[].lines. Commands (clear, home, set DDRAM/CGRAM address) and character writes are tracked; timing, busy flag, CGRAM custom glyphs and display shifting are not modelled."
    },
    {
      "id": "oled_ssd1306",
      "name": "OLED 128x64 (SSD1306, I2C)",
      "category": "Display",
      "subcategory": "OLED",
      "description": "Monochrome 0.96\" OLED display, I2C 4-pin interface.",
      "keywords": ["oled", "ssd1306", "128x64", "i2c", "display"],
      "protocols": ["I2C"],
      "interfaces": ["I2C"],
      "pins": [
        {"name": "VCC", "type": "power"}, {"name": "GND", "type": "ground"},
        {"name": "SCL", "type": "input"}, {"name": "SDA", "type": "bidirectional"}
      ],
      "model": {"shape": "oled_i2c"},
      "mounting": "module",
      "simulation_status": "external",
      "simulation_models": ["ssd1306-gddram"],
      "simulation_backend": "firmware",
      "arduino_compatible": true,
      "params": {
        "address": {"default": 60, "label": "I2C address (7-bit)"},
        "cols": {"default": 128, "label": "Columns", "min": 1, "max": 256},
        "pages": {"default": 8, "label": "Pages (8 rows each)", "min": 1, "max": 16}
      },
      "notes": "No breadboard electrical model: the harness decodes the SSD1306 command/data stream from I2C writes into the GDDRAM frame and returns it in run_firmware's devices[].pages_hex (plus pixels_set and display_on). Command/data are distinguished by the control byte (bit6 = D/C), and page/horizontal/vertical addressing with the 0x21/0x22 range commands is tracked, so a driver's frame writes land correctly. Not modelled: the panel optics, contrast/charge-pump effects, scrolling and the 0x2E/0x2F hardware scroll, and text (there is no font in the harness)."
    },
    {
      "id": "oled_ssd1306_spi",
      "name": "OLED 128x64 (SSD1306, SPI)",
      "category": "Display",
      "subcategory": "OLED",
      "description": "Monochrome OLED display with a 7-pin SPI interface.",
      "keywords": ["oled", "ssd1306", "spi", "128x64", "display"],
      "protocols": ["SPI"],
      "interfaces": ["SPI"],
      "pins": [
        {"name": "GND", "type": "ground"}, {"name": "VCC", "type": "power"},
        {"name": "D0", "type": "clock"}, {"name": "D1", "type": "bidirectional"},
        {"name": "RES", "type": "input"}, {"name": "DC", "type": "input"}, {"name": "CS", "type": "input"}
      ],
      "model": {"shape": "oled_spi"},
      "mounting": "module",
      "simulation_status": "external",
      "simulation_models": ["ssd1306-spi-gddram"],
      "simulation_backend": "firmware",
      "arduino_compatible": true,
      "params": {
        "cols": {"default": 128, "label": "Columns", "min": 1, "max": 256},
        "pages": {"default": 8, "label": "Pages (8 rows each)", "min": 1, "max": 16}
      },
      "notes": "No breadboard electrical model: the harness taps the ATmega's SPI peripheral (so a sketch must use the hardware SPI pins, MOSI = D11 / SCK = D13 - a bit-banged bus is not visible to it) and decodes the SSD1306 command/data stream into the GDDRAM frame, returned in run_firmware's devices[].pages_hex (plus pixels_set and display_on). Command vs data comes from the panel's DC line and CS marks the selected transaction; wire DC and CS to virtual pins and map them with pin_map ({\"9\": \"P1\", ...}) exactly as for a sensor, since attach_devices resolves them from the netlist. Addressing (page/horizontal/vertical, 0x21/0x22 ranges, B0-B7 column set) is shared with the I2C variant. Not modelled: the panel optics, contrast/charge-pump effects, scrolling and text (there is no font in the harness)."
    },
